Project Summary
The Northern Nigeria Education Initiative Plus (NEI+) project works to improve the quality of and access to education in Northern Nigeria, equitably and sustainably.
Position Summary
The EMIS Specialist will provide technical assistance on education information management systems project-wide.
Reporting & Supervision:
This position is housed in Abuja, Nigeria, reporting to the System Strengthening Specialist.
Primary Responsibilities
Support the development of a common web-based EMIS using existing open source software that can be customized by state and LGEAs to meet unique information needs;
Provide ongoing technical support to ministries, departments, and agencies staff to review progress, “trouble shoot” problems, and support use of EMIS data;
Provide support for inter-state training for SMOE, SUBEB, and planners, analysts, and policy makers focused on gathering, analyzing and using data from the EMIS, reading assessments, evaluations, and research to make decisions and plan education improvement initiatives;
Support planners and policy makers to use data for quality decision-making
Provide assistance in setting up systems to gather data for access to quality education and support EGR related data at the state level.
Required Skills & Qualifications
At least 6 years of work experience with EMIS with international development organizations or in an international development context;
Experience in data collection procedures, systems design, systems analysis, and information systems project management;
Demonstrated ability to create and manage a large, secure web-based EMIS systems and software;
Fluency in English;
Master's degree or higher in Statistics, Demography, ICT, Management Information Systems (MIS), or related field required.

Multilateral Liaison Field Officer (Humanitarian Affairs Adviser 1) provides support to the ICRC Delegation in
understanding and influencing the humanitarian environment in Nigeria. S/He also helps shaping the engagement of the
Delegation with the ECOWAS and other international and civil society organizations.
Main duties and responsibilities
Develops strategies and plans of action for ICRC’s engagement with ECOWAS and implements them;
Reinforce the ICRC’s network of interlocutors at ECOWAS and within international organizations working with ECOWAS;
Promotes International Humanitarian Law and ICRC thematic issues of concern with the ECOWAS and within international organisations working with ECOWAS;
Initiates and organises events with key Commissions and Directorates in ECOWAS and the diplomatic community;
Collects and analyses relevant information in order to identify the emerging actors and issues within ECOWAS, so as to enable, if required, an adequate positioning of the institution;
Conducts analyses of the general multilateral environment in Abuja Nigeria, and in West Africa;
Identifies, participates in and/or organises relevant events (e.g. conferences, workshops, meetings) on multilateral issues of concern to the ICRC and represent the ICRC when required;
Facilitates regular exchange of information between the Delegation in Abuja and other Delegations in ECOWAS Member States/the ICRC’s Delegation to the African Union (AU) as well as with HQ in Geneva.
Education and experience required
Masters degree in Law, Diplomacy, International Relations or closely related fields;
Very good knowledge of international humanitarian law (IHL) and international affairs;
Minimum 4 years work experience in multilateral field with governmental, international organizations, or NGO;
Excellent command of written and spoken English and good knowledge of French;
Knowledge of treaty implementation or governmental/parliamentary law-making processes.
Personal Attributes:
Excellent networking and diplomatic skills;
Very good drafting as well as analytical reporting capacities;
Very strong capacities to develop strategies and plan of actions and to implement them;
Ability to handle various thematic files in a transversal manner;
Capacity to work in a team, but also to act independently and to take initiative;
Excellent communication skills; able to represent ICRC and ICRC institutional positions to external audiences.
